    <title>[LIVE!] Place Version History in Studio</title>
    <link>https://devforum.roblox.com/t/live-place-version-history-in-studio/607597</link>
    <description>Hey everyone,

Place Version History is now available for everyone! Before you jump in, we have created a new workflow that&#39;s important to understand, so check out the steps below!

1. Open up Place Version History
1a. At the time of this writing, use Game Explorer, Asset Manager, or Game Settings to open up Place Version History.

(Game Explorer)
![image|542x160, 50%](upload://qLtkpN3wEcBNGXC92rUK7VbvOJD.png) 

(Asset Manager)
![image|690x367, 50%](upload://kEfuJGPxElaAYMO9pGZZRwaFFlO.png) 

(Game Settings)
![image|690x95, 75%](upload://8OfxEevVlS83mN9rLKxRFqhv8gV.png) 
![image|688x146, 50%](upload://xD7TO8ASr3PJscXXAVlE87CUXZD.png) 

2. This will open up the Version History panel
![image|690x402, 75%](upload://4wJpNGBQL6Vhqs4sKeQejCECr3l.png) 

3. Select the version you want to view. This will download the place version locally and open it up. 
4. From here, either copy over the contents you wish to retrieve or publish over the place entirely.
4a. **Caveat:** If your game has Team Create enabled, please make sure all users leave the session before saving/publishing!
4b. You have complete agency over what place your overwrite or if you want to create a new place or game with this content. 

Report any issues you see in the thread! We are currently working on documentation and will update this post once that is released.

Before signing off, I&#39;d like to give a huge shout out to @RainingSwordFire, @PoshKiwi, @tamtamchu  and @chilliflakes19</description>
